Trt_Concerns_Desc:
The purpose of Action is to stabilize and rehabilitate the area burned by the Holloway Fire, including:
1. minimize threats to life or property (rangeland and related range improvements; safety from potential flood and debris flows, etc.);
2. protect cultural resources from looting or vandalism;
3. stabilize soils and reduce offsite soil loss by establishing ground cover of desirable perennial vegetation in order to compete with annual grasses and noxious weeds, reduce the likelihood of new weed establishment, reduce the potential for accelerated soil erosion (both wind and water), reduce sediment deposition into fish bearing streams and promote the recovery of sage-grouse habitat;
4. reduce the risk of noxious weed and annual grass infestations through Early Detection/Rapid Response (EDRR);
5. protect road resources by preventing degradation and allowing continued water flow;
6. reduce the risk of rock and soil movement from the burned area, downslope onto roadways;
7. protect burned areas from livestock grazing until objectives ( 3 desirable plants m/2) are met;
8. reduce fine fuels within the burned area to protect the area and wildlife habitat from future high intensity wildfire;
9. repair or replace damaged facilities needed for management of livestock, including fences and spring developments; and continue to provide water sources for wildlife.
10. protect remote infrastructure (powerlines, powerpoles, wells, etc) from future damage caused by wildfires.

